# Testing

Vitest for unit and integration tests. Playwright for end-to-end tests. Put shared builders and fixtures in `packages/test-utils`; do not duplicate setup in individual specs.

Every feature change includes tests plus error handling, logging, and documentation. Prefer:

- Unit tests for domain invariants and pure application logic
- Integration tests for Prisma repositories, HTTP adapters, and worker handlers against real Postgres/MinIO where the repo provides them
- E2E tests for critical signer and sender journeys against the local stack (Postgres via Compose, filesystem object storage shared by API and worker)

Do not hit production services. Do not assert on secrets, raw tokens, or full PII in logs or snapshots. Playwright traces and screenshots are retained on failure only; signing tokens are redacted from those artifacts where practical.

E2E specs are tagged `@smoke`, `@regression`, `@security`, and `@resilience`. Isolate data per test with new opaque ids. Poll observable state with a deadline (`pollUntil`); do not use arbitrary sleeps.

Playwright `e2e/support` may use Prisma only for test-only fault injection (expired sessions, audit-chain corruption, injected transaction failures). That is not application or React code; UI still must not import Prisma.

```typescript
// ❌ BAD — untested claim, hidden clock, sequential IDs
it('sends', async () => { await sendEnvelope(input); });

// ✅ GOOD — fixture + frozen clock + opaque ids
it('records an append-only audit event on send', async () => {
  const envelope = envelopeBuilder().readyToSend().build();
  const result = await sendEnvelope(envelope, { clock: frozenClock });
  expect(result.audit).toHaveLength(1);
});
```

Never claim tests passed unless the exact command was executed in this session. Report the command, outcome, and anything not covered.
